<title>CHILE: Codelco El Teniente copper pit in wage talks.</title>
<headline>Codelco El Teniente copper pit in wage talks.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Management and unions at Chilean state company Codelco's El Teniente copper mine are in talks on a new collective contract to replace the existing pact which expires at the end of December.</p>
<p>&quot;The negotiations have been brought forward as there are national (parliamentary) elections at the end of the year,&quot; an official at the mine told Reuters.</p>
<p>Unions and management had agreed to early talks to prevent the negotiations from being dragged into local political campaigns, he said.  </p>
<p>Around 6,000 workers at the pit, Codelco's second largest division, are involved in the talks.</p>
<p>El Teniente mined 342,800 tonnes of copper last year.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
